 res←dmx HandleError req;NL;URLEncode;body;detail;json;link;params;repo;reqline;status;suspend;title;⎕IO
⍝ Stark's OnErrorFn (registered in Run.aplf): converts any error raised while
⍝ servicing a request into the HTTP response.
⍝   dmx: the ⎕DMX caught by Stark
⍝   req: the request object (Fail / Method / Endpoint / QueryParams)
⍝ Every error answers the same envelope, so a client can format the parts it wants:
⍝   error message request query_parameters, plus detail and report_url on a 500.
 NL←⎕UCS 10
⍝ How many classes of error suspend (default to production if not yet configured)
 suspend←0
 :If 2=GLOBAL.⎕NC'suspend'
     suspend←GLOBAL.suspend
 :EndIf
 :If dmx.Vendor≡'DCMS'                             ⍝ Expected error deliberately signalled.
     Log'[ERR] ',⍕dmx.(EN Vendor Message)
     detail←dmx.Message
     :If 0∊⍴detail                                 ⍝ fall back to the diagnostic message lines
         detail←1↓∊NL,¨dmx.DM
     :EndIf
     status←500                                    ⍝ server-side expected error
     :If (dmx.EN≥400)∧(dmx.EN<600)                 ⍝ client error → respond with that status
         status←dmx.EN
     :EndIf
     res←(error:status ⋄ message:detail)
 :Else                                             ⍝ Unexpected error.
     Log'[ERR] ',⍕dmx.(EN Vendor Message DM)
     :If 1=suspend                                ⍝ development: leave the bug to suspend
         ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' dmx.EN)('EM' dmx.EM)('Message' dmx.Message)
     :EndIf
    ⍝ suspend=0 (production): turn the bug into a generic 500 + a pre-filled issue link
    ⍝ Percent-encode a character vector (UTF-8) for use in a URL query value
     URLEncode←{
         unreserved←'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-_.~'
         hex←'0123456789ABCDEF'
         ⎕IO←0
         ∊{(⎕UCS ⍵)∊unreserved:⎕UCS ⍵ ⋄ '%',hex[16 16⊤⍵]}¨'UTF-8'⎕UCS ⍵
     }
     repo←'https://github.com/Dyalog/DCMS'
     reqline←req.Method,' ',req.Endpoint
     params←1 ⎕JSON req.QueryParams                ⍝ {} when no query parameters
     detail←dmx.Message
     :If 0∊⍴detail                                 ⍝ unexpected errors often carry no Message
         detail←dmx.EM                             ⍝ error name only; DM would leak source lines
     :EndIf
     json←1 ⎕JSON ⎕OPT'Compact' 0⊢dmx              ⍝ full, uncompacted error details
     ⎕←'[ERR] ',json                               ⍝ Stays server-side. Not via Log: production sets logging 0
     ⍝ Pre-fill a GitHub issue with the request context
     title←'API error: ',reqline
     body←'**Request:** ',reqline,NL,NL
     body,←'**Query parameters:** ',params,NL,NL
     body,←'**Error message:** ',detail,NL,NL
     body,←'Please describe what you were doing when this happened.'
     link←repo,'/issues/new?title=',(URLEncode title),'&body=',(URLEncode body)
     status←500
     res←(error:status ⋄ message:'There was an error processing your request.')
     res.detail←detail
     res.report_url←link
 :EndIf
⍝ Request context, on every error
 res.request←(method:req.Method ⋄ endpoint:req.Endpoint)
 res.query_parameters←⎕NS req.QueryParams          ⍝ Copy: the response must not alias the request
 req.Fail status
